amdgpu: do not query RAS capability from a VBIOS that is not there

amdgpu_ras_init() -> amdgpu_ras_check_supported() ->
amdgpu_ras_query_ras_capablity_from_vbios() ->
amdgpu_atomfirmware_mem_ecc_supported() -> amdgpu_atom_parse_data_header()
dereferences adev->mode_info.atom_context, which is NULL on a device with
no VBIOS image: an emulated gfx1250 (rocjitsu) here.  The probe oopses.

Not a v7.4 change: the in-tree driver at v7.4-rc3 has the same path and
the same oops.  Needed to probe the emulated GPU with either.

--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ras.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ras.c
@@ -3379,6 +3379,10 @@
 /* Query ras capablity via atomfirmware interface */
 static void amdgpu_ras_query_ras_capablity_from_vbios(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
+	/* A device without a VBIOS image has nothing to ask. */
+	if (!adev->mode_info.atom_context)
+		return;
+
 	/* mem_ecc cap */
 	if (amdgpu_atomfirmware_mem_ecc_supported(adev)) {
 		dev_info(adev->dev, "MEM ECC is active.\n");
